[{"id":"VRCE-4-18-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":1,"english":"And thus Rāma was addressed by Vāli, wounded and senseless, with those modest, pious and auspicious words. And being thus reproached he spoke to that excellent lord of monkeys, gifted with virtue and other accomplishments, resembling the Sun shorn of its lustre, a cloud which has already discharged its waters and fire extinguished.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"deb4927e2ac261729579ffc33aaf6c61e3355500c3d191c936cee31917195b7a","compact":"3d14e8ffffaf735ec6eb407fc3d71f18664b03dce822d89f4b7d9b5b0f3c8e25","nasal":"b79396dd4f15fac4893bf2eae5f5f9c417bdb40e6ea5bc8b6e7c2dd1e90478b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":2,"english":"And thus Rāma was addressed by Vāli, wounded and senseless, with those modest, pious and auspicious words. And being thus reproached he spoke to that excellent lord of monkeys, gifted with virtue and other accomplishments, resembling the Sun shorn of its lustre, a cloud which has already discharged its waters and fire extinguished.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b6c4d8cb2ebd9bc7fdcd99095b861af187548f6b8f7898a3530ff6faf426c4d8","compact":"0081a884d65f1ef01523b016ca5109d30c9b9fa90ba334881c20e4a25baf93fa","nasal":"76aa5bada368dd0aeeaad074011e3e9a6ca46adfc05c1064c98c88d13b70e6e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":3,"english":"And thus Rāma was addressed by Vāli, wounded and senseless, with those modest, pious and auspicious words. And being thus reproached he spoke to that excellent lord of monkeys, gifted with virtue and other accomplishments, resembling the Sun shorn of its lustre, a cloud which has already discharged its waters and fire extinguished.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.894,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74499b1378b21db06fbb20a82a61057873cf30d321d09130a5c962592fc9ece7","compact":"b2fdbee1321016c9e3c255753257d25e35bb0e66dda57d09a01b20de79d3a133","nasal":"34fc7b00b0d85bd19ca51e333d919c86f4fc5fb381122af7bb26fb9b485404ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":4,"english":"Not cognizant of virtue, knowledge, passion and custom, why did you blame me like a child?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0363386f7886a9454759a17cf624f1e02e1849c54e73f4ccf5a7e6cdeca7c1ae","compact":"fb5d4176f590225135b4e3ef09f77204ba6bc39bdaaea1cdcd12a32fd58f49dd","nasal":"fb5d4176f590225135b4e3ef09f77204ba6bc39bdaaea1cdcd12a32fd58f49dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":5,"english":"Why did you purpose to address me thus out of fickleness, consequent upon your monkeyhood not asking your wise elders recognized by the preceptors?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"943585de73cba654b8a48b8c7c9659e3577dbe5f8ff82333e81c7d6e2e806f44","compact":"9fd92419bc286fc5ef920d4b380020f9670c57ff141e55beab7a8379211daf4e","nasal":"536b191e8040da6c27d42d0abe8631fe24175e32bf4b8f0ea45f424d47bd51bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":6,"english":"This land, abounding in hills and woods, belongs to the lkşwakus. Along with it was conferred on them the power of administering favour and chastisement to beasts, birds and human beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c4d9d23b637ecc7cccbbb069e561bb49a9c756865d9c554f867390808d02d4a3","compact":"c8196f9ceb5ac799acf266b352ddd906937aee5d7a8cb2de6baded0ebe66b74e","nasal":"c8196f9ceb5ac799acf266b352ddd906937aee5d7a8cb2de6baded0ebe66b74e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":7,"english":"The upright, virtuous and truthful king Bharata, cognizant of virtue, knowledge and passion and ever engaged in administering favour and punisl.ment, governs this kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e9300607642fc482b2f456c90af2a079f7a4cbf74983aea7961346127556bde","compact":"4c705c16b3e65215f596fae2a292644f17debe8981f9bd04574ac68cc4f58ad8","nasal":"4c705c16b3e65215f596fae2a292644f17debe8981f9bd04574ac68cc4f58ad8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":8,"english":"That king is said to be cognizant of time and place; in him dwelleth modesty, truthfulness, prowess and a love for discipline.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7a08d0d35aa8eb58608ddf35d493f7e09d0b242beed0091d259548f412ed790","compact":"4b51b09fc21c5969c128b4c3daed5024b5ae817dfef575fc6c2bbee107805d70","nasal":"4b51b09fc21c5969c128b4c3daed5024b5ae817dfef575fc6c2bbee107805d70"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":9,"english":"Ourselves and other kings, being commanded by him to practise piety, have been journeying in this wide world desirous of multiplying virtue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d00d101212c6abffd40b705bbfad08d5b8b8e501d8956031b6060087a8abf7f","compact":"5cbdcf2f74d28beb8fc44579498d9745a9b4eee32d909d31388a433dcf2a0b3c","nasal":"5cbdcf2f74d28beb8fc44579498d9745a9b4eee32d909d31388a433dcf2a0b3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":10,"english":"That foremost of monarchs, Bharatalover of virtue, governing this entire earth, who dares perpetrate an iniquity.?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ffb7101528d08a8dbc7f6ffa331f1f0f634de30d80d7332783a08da21185ec1","compact":"6f2a12a416a976758f50892de65cca31db2b9ab6728c7be843bae75bf8ce9154","nasal":"a8af1eff87f81f1507a09a533b883427321dbc11bc5468097073ef2354a68103"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":11,"english":"Stationed in the excellent virtue of our own and placing Bharata's commandments on our heads, we shall consider how we shall punish them who go astray (from the path of virtue).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.537,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c2998e8ddf89fe26a0effc1120d6ac05e732c42f86650d28dcd1bbcade29d22","compact":"c84a5f0ffb1bd44337deb6266bb6e46c84f17a7b090428338246d3abd8c72f7d","nasal":"c84a5f0ffb1bd44337deb6266bb6e46c84f17a7b090428338246d3abd8c72f7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":12,"english":"You have oppressed virtue and perpetrated a gross iniquity. You have placed yourself under the control of your passions and deviated from the track of royal duties.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2cd14cb30cbc811f9916a76b579b42578577d22004fa8e73d1029023ed5e42ac","compact":"06448cc6f5799c50af16ded66c097a458811f972ef76220dc258c6486ebe6b5a","nasal":"b7e2ddddaa6174863bba42e9d79ee829773a1f16f1458654fc4336f98587b85c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":13,"english":"The elder brother, father, and the instructor—these three should always be regarded in the light of a father if they tread the paths of virtue and morality,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.739,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e068cc53c6da229a06a7a8bf84407206a904ca525fca65534818c4c4b9dfd4cf","compact":"80b77dc68ebadd69e095f5e4a1bde7af44487abf7d65a978dc5838678d9ecfaa","nasal":"80b77dc68ebadd69e095f5e4a1bde7af44487abf7d65a978dc5838678d9ecfaa"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":14,"english":"A younger brother, a son and an accomplished follower should always be regarded as sons. And virtue is always at the bottom of all such considerations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9a82c3a0251be3a3ed8dc67633470d703a23e68ff61309a87beee6045ac0d31a","compact":"75ff0c20993f616a0478070c0ef0c854076bd115fc74ec29116a373a129e9cc7","nasal":"df67d3568e32db60b8db7f078d9e5aec04be5fc3626b6d8f0e4f99d3bc7e8dfa"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":15,"english":"O monkey, the religion of the good is indeed very subtle and can comprehend great things the immortal soul can understand what is good or bad.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"98f26704a1ec113e940f378e3a7ca220d7fa16abeb412099144ea58a76fd21e7","compact":"f0f26112cf9443c4c31375ebd2ed2bdeec329c0e258a75d500dd44423305405c","nasal":"f0f26112cf9443c4c31375ebd2ed2bdeec329c0e258a75d500dd44423305405c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":16,"english":"Fickle as you are, how canst you comprehend what is proper, consulting with your monkey companions who are equally stupid and lighthearted, like to one, born blind, leading with another such?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3f82b0121c6166d2d50dd3c215508a737e263a865ff5c31606568fa46ffde60","compact":"e5915d9052c019c8fcfe809cb99511ae56f1ccab012abd0d03379c306e760ddb","nasal":"f93d34ade8b3f3369a17b3f91e00de323114c5a510445c13d17a8cfa6e08431c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":17,"english":"I do fairly speak to you that it is not anger only that has led me to bring about your destruction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7bd97021a4d705be0e1d42531a6ecfb5de73d600d29b148188d85c97677be33e","compact":"25c138b7dbf0075ae6af25812cca921ae400aa8230dad7ad7aa2095dc91bd2ef","nasal":"25c138b7dbf0075ae6af25812cca921ae400aa8230dad7ad7aa2095dc91bd2ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":18,"english":"Do you consider why I have killed you-you had ravished your brother's wife renouncing that ever-existing virtue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"251869aaa31d992c61f73f689e98c7141ab8bea65dce5a74a18b56ecc494b5bf","compact":"1d762fa874792ecff8a4bcd50a97663f6e29644bfa428b7fd912dc84e5de5348","nasal":"1d762fa874792ecff8a4bcd50a97663f6e29644bfa428b7fd912dc84e5de5348"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":19,"english":"You, the perpetrator of many evil deeds, have got by Rumā, the wife of your brother-the high-souled Sugrīva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e55db2f2298beab47969844fe67cee06d22a9210216c84713e46c1ad32c863d0","compact":"174c2dc681f09b73eb7e90b23869e4521fdb106354c10114d390f7328ea61274","nasal":"174c2dc681f09b73eb7e90b23869e4521fdb106354c10114d390f7328ea61274"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":20,"english":"O monkey, you had thus violated the path of virtue. And thus I have punished you who have ravished your elder brother's spouse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.861,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbbcc563e5b5722daf5c4780d78df4bb7e980bc4c5e73c55ad8c6a0545dbedae","compact":"3ffb1194fd38974ad69456717f3ac406cac8cad493f9304dc7eaa271ade792ae","nasal":"85312991d26e286e1c6f0b53db9ee263f0d657d05f4a27872bca523a44e43d84"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":21,"english":"o you, the leader of monkey-herds-I find no other alternative than to punish him who act against humanity and violates the sacred sanctions of custom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b41f541e5cb8ba16e4d2e78d5eb59853daae6799864dbe75d55af87451dae033","compact":"09ddc4391ceb1391633d8b6cb5b0346a748dd4351165ad8bc7f1cb7314eb2f9e","nasal":"18bbcdf3917338b30455da7aaa91996f926cfb723c0ef4e1d04944f9283c9060"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":22,"english":"I am a Ksatrya coming of a high pedigree. I cannot put up with your immoral conduct. Šāstras sanction the destruction of one who under the influence of passion ravishes his own daughter, sister and younger brother's wife.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6bb4f011a18b982012b14787dc3ac06cd02d10e75a09248bafc086d58429668c","compact":"af726a3ebfadd26bdfcecb3a180adffcd4db7ac2290c0d3ee1ef7f301d063b7d","nasal":"7ade0e452c24da3784a7e4b1ac41b1c0a77a8f24219f7d854b455f1dd48b9d2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":23,"english":"This is Bharata's commandment-the lord of earth, and we have been satisfying his orders. You have disregarded virtue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de106afcd84ed9852da9bef750fce290b87812ec8024fea9c128603ca0368c65","compact":"5a64b84a0ad595a0dfa8eb15ff80b950e8a1b1b39e1ab17b09178174f1f3b723","nasal":"8a0af6e3f4d3f9eba79e67c93f547dc6f991fb98728137015322ac62693c7017"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":24,"english":"A wise man, living in virtue, cannot let go one who has passed by the sanctions of morality. Bharata has sanctioned the destruction of the amorous; and we, O lord of monkeys, following his orders, thought proper, to encompass the destruction of one like you who has spoliated virtue and morality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a128765ebe31f39ea302d4e9ea193dda91f311c8ed9a41c6d17642102441e34","compact":"1305e1aba6753053ae0dfe64ab10aba17f5a272d92defba30bc5dee88bc1a11a","nasal":"6dcd47abd0d7bfea877e7e4563805c85fb9a88e319c0cabb468d462128607a8c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":25,"english":"A wise man, living in virtue, cannot let go one who has passed by the sanctions of morality. Bharata has sanctioned the destruction of the amorous; and we, O lord of monkeys, following his orders, thought proper, to encompass the destruction of one like you who has spoliated virtue and morality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7ec82ba667de57863250b456b8225eddb12e0afacd722b1b77d9e8d52d08855","compact":"26d745318780c718349cdf70ba1505314cf61adc5f2e8f9e73bf3c3e33a56c39","nasal":"6cbe7fa5a9c2a575f389211ed15f476637153045894506727ba73aa9bb17048f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":26,"english":"Like to Laksmana, I have contracted friendship with Sugrīva. And with a view to regain his wife and kingdom, he resolved to engage in my well-being. I too also promised the same before the monkeys. And how can a man of my position neglect to make good his promise?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a06b221a97f74ba24c3a9966b9caa44a337995af2727839896ba493f75783c86","compact":"53ec775bd69fd8b16488079b651b5c07fee8b95b8e6c02fbff0dd4ad1e5ab506","nasal":"53ec775bd69fd8b16488079b651b5c07fee8b95b8e6c02fbff0dd4ad1e5ab506"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":27,"english":"Like to Laksmana, I have contracted friendship with Sugrīva. And with a view to regain his wife and kingdom, he resolved to engage in my well-being. I too also promised the same before the monkeys. And how can a man of my position neglect to make good his promise?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b17d87b146799fbbb67057fc546323ebdd6f0cda1028339e9277d586a138ccd6","compact":"d349c48b59e6c715f353a4363fdd2e8385ae79bc0f7f3a0393268f2f3120b406","nasal":"d349c48b59e6c715f353a4363fdd2e8385ae79bc0f7f3a0393268f2f3120b406"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":28,"english":"For these causes of very great moment, favoured by virtue, I have adininistered to you this condign punishment. Do you now approve it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"62442160373930aae993583dab2eefc1a48764cf41b82e65ed3d6864b9d40a1d","compact":"6ff3699dd036454ccac51fc1fa8c94563a55fa94d9e16a429a13045654099d5a","nasal":"6ff3699dd036454ccac51fc1fa8c94563a55fa94d9e16a429a13045654099d5a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-29","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":29,"english":"Your discomfiture is quite of a piece with the sanctions of morality-and to assist friends in one of the codes of religion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2410b2b9976b749a382c6c77ba568815292c4f654050c364780936ca7f6a7742","compact":"a742f6b5a58f141f682c1530efa1b0f7168223da3c5d90681e3a1147b7ba0913","nasal":"a742f6b5a58f141f682c1530efa1b0f7168223da3c5d90681e3a1147b7ba0913"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":30,"english":"Those who, perpetrating iniquity, bear with fortitude the punishment, inflicted by their sovereign get at the abode of the celestials being purified like to the pious. People are freed from their sins, when they confessing their crimes, are either punished or forgiven. But the monarch who does not punish the perpetrator of an evil deed, is visited by a mighty sin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"777c007f961154b013026b4dd1d290851fdd0c8ea238fc0ca343c5d7605253bd","compact":"9edca0fe12e6b189b412cbe8f98a4cd3079fee03d10d175509f5c890fe31e479","nasal":"18090bd6a642d2ed07b1086e083ba2b9e2fb1aab488ae1396820d3ede9062d5b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":31,"english":"Formerly an iniquity, like one perpetrated by you, was committed by a devotee who was punished severely by my forefather Māndhäta.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0eeb4e8e1a98480ca3ff865728551b60f85d492eed1bcc57ea6c170b1e93c851","compact":"0c20c0edcfb78deb34c3d6f97e206e70bc97a83543d7313d3815a8490651d814","nasal":"6e7bbe84dd5a67f25d59c3af6654c4d15e63cc1597f36024b8c21c84e5a5d8f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":32,"english":"And other lords of earth punish in the same way the authors of misdeeds. What more, the perpetrators of crime, themselves undergo penances and are thus released from their sins.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8276329df58fac4affaaf7294ec628efdb848c509e432e41b58b086d6bccd245","compact":"ba84967b1fd43f95c3e4ee20f3d566dfdf0db2cf5d19f67eeee1ec3928793427","nasal":"e5d40fb63e6286270bb46afeddf8ecb9cafd7afcd28896f3e5e048997c02734a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":33,"english":"Therefore do not repent any more, O best of monkeys. The punishment, I have inflicted on you, is in consonance with the sanctions of morality. We are not our own masters.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ecd6a7642afe4741368a1257b00e0b3a645df1b9fc7bec614cd715077800650","compact":"a01cea10c998f8ff9619235ad096b59050aff602eacf58cc2bd1143c22060316","nasal":"a01cea10c998f8ff9619235ad096b59050aff602eacf58cc2bd1143c22060316"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":34,"english":"Many persons living on flesh, either lying in ambush, or openly catch and pierce by means of net, noose and trap, many a deer, terrified and trusted, taking to their heels or quarrelling with their companions, careful or careless. They are not to blame in this and I do not cherish, O best of monkeys, any mortification or ire for this.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a8b44a9266a99a46072e7eff59838f16636a3b26685a1bd07a00135b6b6528c","compact":"a34eaef52b12d46da12b63aed8c1e18a08b669d9d63d8c3765f3ff468a0813ad","nasal":"3c5ed9c7d50341f8c77b8373ef98c2a12161e12d9c113f21db9838fbc269b8ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-35","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":35,"english":"And even many royal ascetics, versed in religious lore, go a-hunting; and hence you had been killed by me with a shaft, O monkey, in the conflict.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018035","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b855f14d00196e78be8dcd67e1d64c1e8513b4978a95855491c77de90db99c3a","compact":"fda9a3facd82e52f027d3bdf54f8206378822e0210ea41cdd21ddb274b146b52","nasal":"2c7ce319829615d9925c26c7a3a7a1c0f59feaa180506a8024dd6db136ad01f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-36","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":36,"english":"And I am justified in killing you, whether you did fight or not since you are a monkey. There is no doubt, O best monkeys, that the monarchs confer life and piety auspicious and hard to attain. It does not therefore behove any one to injure them, to blame them and to use improper words by them-since they are the celestials ranging on this earth under the semblance of man.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.925,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018036","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19c4111ac83831db7c2fffed6cb7fc774d44505615df6b0498b8d432936e41b6","compact":"27460ab330aa76c16a70007464d6b6c11d35265dc9b67f96bedeac6d7de5371c","nasal":"c407bfe814beca5b9c99232e5c7662e3242406d225ed1e3d0daa9c9906acfbb5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-37","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":37,"english":"And I am justified in killing you, whether you did fight or not since you are a monkey. There is no doubt, O best monkeys, that the monarchs confer life and piety auspicious and hard to attain. It does not therefore behove any one to injure them, to blame them and to use improper words by them-since they are the celestials ranging on this earth under the semblance of man.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018037","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01f7983a7a18946326344e700d1a057991fd801ee53d8c8e1f673933b0415878","compact":"3fab9dc4a408c9c414116f1ccc6e98d5f3e9b638dbb2d387615e58f5d8971635","nasal":"3fab9dc4a408c9c414116f1ccc6e98d5f3e9b638dbb2d387615e58f5d8971635"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-38","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":38,"english":"And I am justified in killing you, whether you did fight or not since you are a monkey. There is no doubt, O best monkeys, that the monarchs confer life and piety auspicious and hard to attain. It does not therefore behove any one to injure them, to blame them and to use improper words by them-since they are the celestials ranging on this earth under the semblance of man.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018038","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2bd44e282a34a804dfc62aea0dbdf60a387484d55714cad9febfe24e9a52b7db","compact":"6c5cc8fbfc1b1f2a1dab850bdbe3f894563bddbd750837a9653b1559f60a007e","nasal":"f59a8b4fbad6c3a1c7fe97708075c6252bc3b01fa24023ef43c502cca6d8cb13"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-39","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":39,"english":"Not knowing virtue and growing angry why did you blame me who am following the religion of my forefathers?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018039","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae47aca3d22bf9205320a3fea86541475df8491f5d3340a8ddef6dd745638574","compact":"ac1b84008b805975b79869358efeda481fcdda661b569b83484d66fede1fedfb","nasal":"ac1b84008b805975b79869358efeda481fcdda661b569b83484d66fede1fedfb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-40","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":40,"english":"Being thus accosted by Rāma, Vāli, greatly mortified and informed of the principle of religion, observed no delinquency in Rāghava. Thereupon that lord of monkeys spoke to Răma, with folded hands, saying:-There is not the least doubt, О best of men, in all that you had said.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.47,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-36","DUTT-4-18-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018040","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae2140f508bced7247378284cd58113e66e60aea530d704f108fde727228c43c","compact":"591fb036b5d3a6aa2d60b1f474c05f6d209198ff08f51693febdd6df3ee54fc3","nasal":"185c9535d6204b27efb0db98f8f3ce5f09e686881a1a6e603c04af82dfdd61ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-41","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":41,"english":"An inferior person can by no means address his superior improperly. It does not behove you, O Rāghava, therefore to blame me for those unpleasant words which I used towards you, out of foolishness. You have acquired a practical mastery over the principles of religion and are ever engaged in the welfare of your subjects. Your eternal power of ascertaining the crime and meeting its condign punishment is perfectly clear.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.507,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018041","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7d9d3d42b015c02bc54f1b990499d52adf700f7db441b7d90e28ea289ac25cc8","compact":"9e580baa041030444605a8d12ccdf009a5cb18669f996e5d717a2931a0361a5c","nasal":"9e580baa041030444605a8d12ccdf009a5cb18669f996e5d717a2931a0361a5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-42","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":42,"english":"An inferior person can by no means address his superior improperly. It does not behove you, O Rāghava, therefore to blame me for those unpleasant words which I used towards you, out of foolishness. You have acquired a practical mastery over the principles of religion and are ever engaged in the welfare of your subjects. Your eternal power of ascertaining the crime and meeting its condign punishment is perfectly clear.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018042","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87d23e2265dfe491fb880104793234440cf805215bc1a04ee6c11e1305d82a3d","compact":"ed7596e4b144a8961b7b2200579bc3432f41a3a52a19d812ec52729bd2a4295a","nasal":"ed7596e4b144a8961b7b2200579bc3432f41a3a52a19d812ec52729bd2a4295a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-18-43","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":18,"verse":43,"english":"An inferior person can by no means address his superior improperly. It does not behove you, O Rāghava, therefore to blame me for those unpleasant words which I used towards you, out of foolishness. You have acquired a practical mastery over the principles of religion and are ever engaged in the welfare of your subjects. Your eternal power of ascertaining the crime and meeting its condign punishment is perfectly clear.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.775,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-18-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4018043","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a02a0ce1a137d4cb7d0f97d90a43b811347cc82203351625cbc4e4048f133d05","compact":"6a